// EXAMPLE ONLY -- not wired into any build. Same board as libcamhal_configs.json plus
// isx031-1-selfdiscover.json.example, taken one step further: "autoDiscoverSensors":
// true removes the need for a "sensors/<name>.json" file altogether -- including the
// one-line "discoverSensorEntity" stub -- for every sensor listed in
// "availableSensors". CameraParserInvoker builds each CameraInfo purely from
// SensorNodeDiscovery, deriving the sensor's own subdev entity name ("<sensor
// name> <I2CBus>", e.g. "isx031 a-0" for "isx031-a-0") from the resolved CSI
// port/I2C bus the same way a hand-authored "$I2CBUS" placeholder would (see
// CameraSensorsParser::runAutoDiscovery). A whole new board is therefore added by
// editing only this one file's "availableSensors" list, so long as every sensor's
// graph has already been linked/routed out-of-band (udev/board-init service, or
// kernel default routing) before ipu7-camera-hal starts, and its active output format
// is a self-discoverable "simple yuv" passthrough one (see
// CameraUtils::getPixelFormatFromMBusCode). Bayer/RAW sensors needing ISP/PSys/3A
// tuning still require a hand-authored "sensors/<name>.json" and must not be listed
// here; set "autoDiscoverSensors": false (the default) for boards that mix the two.
//
{
    "Common" : {
        "version": 1.0,
        "platform": "IPU7",
        "autoDiscoverSensors": true,
        //  The value format of availableSensors is "sensor name"-wf/uf-"CSI port ID".
        //  wf is world facing, and uf is user facing.
        "availableSensors": ["isx031-1-0", "isx031-a-0", "isx031-b-2"],
        "videoStreamNum" : 2
    }
}
